1
00:00:05,831 --> 00:00:07,464
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:09,051
(Filming complied with guidelines
for children, youth, and animals.)

3
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:34,983
Look out!

4
00:00:48,338 --> 00:00:50,345
(Episode 4)

5
00:00:54,023 --> 00:00:57,659
You punk, do you know what that money is?

6
00:00:59,511 --> 00:01:01,774
Sir,

7
00:01:02,003 --> 00:01:05,907
without that money, all six of us
will be out on the street.

8
00:01:06,623 --> 00:01:08,258
Please, just give back the money...

9
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,186
you conned out of me, sir.

10
00:01:10,844 --> 00:01:13,249
Conned? Who conned who, you punk?

11
00:01:19,656 --> 00:01:22,388
Conned?

12
00:01:22,413 --> 00:01:24,244
Help me.

13
00:01:26,164 --> 00:01:27,812
Somebody help.

14
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:29,563
Mu Jin, wake up.

15
00:01:29,588 --> 00:01:32,497
Mu Jin, please wake up!

16
00:01:36,511 --> 00:01:39,114
Where is he hurt? What happened?

17
00:01:39,755 --> 00:01:41,874
How bad is it?

18
00:01:42,810 --> 00:01:44,750
How did this even happen?

19
00:01:48,677 --> 00:01:51,556
It's not life-threatening, right?

20
00:02:22,772 --> 00:02:24,465
(Dad)

21
00:02:25,231 --> 00:02:26,877
Dad, let me call you back...

22
00:02:26,902 --> 00:02:28,271
Gyu Rim!

23
00:02:29,516 --> 00:02:30,589
Dad.

24
00:02:32,337 --> 00:02:34,531
Do you have any money on you?

25
00:02:36,969 --> 00:02:39,041
(In Surgery)

26
00:02:55,683 --> 00:02:56,690
Yun Jin.

27
00:03:12,141 --> 00:03:13,504
What's going on?

28
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:15,104
What happened to your face, Dad?

29
00:03:16,378 --> 00:03:18,261
We've lost the house.

30
00:03:18,757 --> 00:03:19,791
What do you mean?

31
00:03:19,817 --> 00:03:21,990
We're about to be out on the street!

32
00:03:22,150 --> 00:03:23,777
What are you talking about?

33
00:03:23,802 --> 00:03:24,842
Well...

34
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:28,953
What is all this?

35
00:03:29,975 --> 00:03:32,829
Overdue notices, final demands,
auction filing, an eviction order!

36
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:36,797
You never come home,
but you smuggled these out just fine.

37
00:03:37,037 --> 00:03:39,413
I knew you'd all lose it if you found out,

38
00:03:39,747 --> 00:03:41,835
so I had someone handle it quietly.

39
00:03:55,190 --> 00:03:57,611
You took out a loan against this house?

40
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:01,158
I was going to pay it all back,

41
00:04:01,479 --> 00:04:03,569
but some punks conned me out of it,

42
00:04:03,594 --> 00:04:05,781
and I went without food or sleep,

43
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:07,413
even staked the place out
to get that money back,

44
00:04:08,047 --> 00:04:10,135
I barely made it out alive.

45
00:04:10,224 --> 00:04:13,110
Turns out they were gangsters.

46
00:04:13,217 --> 00:04:15,035
Nasty tempers,

47
00:04:15,703 --> 00:04:17,502
and scary as all get-out.

48
00:04:19,377 --> 00:04:20,538
So,

49
00:04:21,414 --> 00:04:23,773
do you two have any money?

50
00:04:24,551 --> 00:04:27,390
Even for a security deposit?

51
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,402
For all six of us to move out today...

52
00:04:29,427 --> 00:04:31,690
We'd need at least two bedrooms,

53
00:04:31,825 --> 00:04:33,304
and a bathroom...

54
00:04:33,311 --> 00:04:35,231
Let's just each fend for ourselves.

55
00:04:36,336 --> 00:04:38,649
Since when were we ever
that tight-knit anyway?

56
00:04:38,674 --> 00:04:41,359
You go your way, Gyu Rim goes hers,
and I'll go mine.

57
00:04:41,384 --> 00:04:42,985
Gyu O's all grown up now too,

58
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:45,337
so let's scatter and each
get by on our own.

59
00:04:45,362 --> 00:04:47,728
Then what about Gyu Min and Gyu Seo?

60
00:04:47,753 --> 00:04:49,161
What about the twins?

61
00:04:50,444 --> 00:04:52,751
Since when did you ever look after them?

62
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:55,248
Their mom ran off when they were three,

63
00:04:55,273 --> 00:04:58,236
and you dumped them on Gyu Rim
and washed your hands of them!

64
00:04:59,584 --> 00:05:00,597
That's enough.

65
00:05:01,203 --> 00:05:03,189
Why? Am I making this up?

66
00:05:03,563 --> 00:05:04,716
You need to wake up too.

67
00:05:04,741 --> 00:05:07,274
Ten years of raising them
is more than enough.

68
00:05:07,590 --> 00:05:10,423
I say we drop them at an orphanage,
even now.

69
00:05:11,370 --> 00:05:13,036
Shut your mouth, Han Gyu Yeong.

70
00:05:13,903 --> 00:05:15,864
Leave the kids out of it,

71
00:05:15,984 --> 00:05:17,928
and if anyone's leaving, it's you.

72
00:05:18,317 --> 00:05:20,210
Fine, I'm leaving.

73
00:05:20,356 --> 00:05:22,660
I'm walking out of this wretched house!

74
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:27,561
That temper of hers.

75
00:05:27,721 --> 00:05:30,196
Who does she take after?

76
00:05:31,144 --> 00:05:33,357
You take after me exactly, Gyu Rim.

77
00:05:36,457 --> 00:05:39,620
How long until we have to be out?

78
00:05:41,284 --> 00:05:42,285
Soon.

79
00:05:43,146 --> 00:05:44,431
Right away.

80
00:05:48,744 --> 00:05:50,390
You really don't have any money?

81
00:05:50,575 --> 00:05:53,127
Nothing squirreled away somewhere?

82
00:05:53,549 --> 00:05:54,563
Really?

83
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:56,996
I'll pay you back later
with generous interest.

84
00:05:57,021 --> 00:05:58,303
I'll see what I can do.

85
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:04,056
Gyu Rim, you really are the eldest
of this family.

86
00:06:04,081 --> 00:06:08,129
You know you're my oxygen tank, right?

87
00:06:14,453 --> 00:06:16,386
Seriously...

88
00:06:35,537 --> 00:06:36,738
I'm off.

89
00:06:36,763 --> 00:06:39,061
Have a lovely life together without me.

90
00:06:50,150 --> 00:06:53,137
(Jeong Woo)

91
00:06:54,150 --> 00:06:55,303
Hello?

92
00:07:05,077 --> 00:07:07,482
- Gyu Rim.
- Jeong Woo!

93
00:07:08,537 --> 00:07:10,378
The surgery went well,

94
00:07:10,488 --> 00:07:12,478
and he was moved to a room
a little while ago.

95
00:07:13,563 --> 00:07:15,270
Why was Mu Jin at a construction site?

96
00:07:17,482 --> 00:07:21,114
He wouldn't let me tell you because
he didn't want you to worry.

97
00:07:21,256 --> 00:07:22,877
Mu Jin was thrown out of the house,

98
00:07:24,464 --> 00:07:26,252
and he was working shifts...

99
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:28,846
at a construction site.

100
00:08:01,256 --> 00:08:02,363
Han Gyu Rim?

101
00:08:10,304 --> 00:08:11,703
I'm Mu Jin's sister.

102
00:08:13,718 --> 00:08:17,431
You're saying you didn't know
he was working construction?

103
00:08:18,729 --> 00:08:21,438
He's never lifted a brick in his life,

104
00:08:21,756 --> 00:08:24,010
and the smell of pain patches
must have been all over him.

105
00:08:25,034 --> 00:08:26,828
You had no idea at all?

106
00:08:28,104 --> 00:08:29,918
- Should we sit here?
- Sure.

107
00:08:38,311 --> 00:08:40,835
- What's this smell of pain patches?
- What?

108
00:08:43,213 --> 00:08:46,150
I hurt myself a bit at the gym earlier.

109
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:49,995
You should be careful. Let me see.

110
00:08:50,996 --> 00:08:52,686
- See what?
- Come on, let me see.

111
00:08:52,711 --> 00:08:53,971
It's nothing. Really.

112
00:08:55,044 --> 00:08:57,003
- Is it bad?
- No, I'm fine.

113
00:09:01,997 --> 00:09:04,826
You didn't know he'd left the house
and was living in a tiny rented room?

114
00:09:05,350 --> 00:09:07,306
What do you know about Mu Jin?

115
00:09:07,809 --> 00:09:11,183
He gave up everything for you.

116
00:09:12,897 --> 00:09:14,604
Just let him go.

117
00:09:15,277 --> 00:09:17,208
Mu Jin is more than,

118
00:09:18,263 --> 00:09:20,024
you can handle.

119
00:09:22,684 --> 00:09:25,574
I'm begging you, Han Gyu Rim.

120
00:09:45,156 --> 00:09:50,563
Stop crying, sweetheart.
They said the surgery went well.

121
00:09:51,471 --> 00:09:53,651
It's because of what I said.

122
00:09:54,643 --> 00:09:58,227
I was so angry I said
I hoped he'd break a leg,

123
00:09:58,252 --> 00:09:59,861
and that's why...

124
00:10:00,104 --> 00:10:02,177
This isn't your fault.

125
00:10:02,642 --> 00:10:05,227
I'm telling you, it's not your fault.

126
00:10:05,577 --> 00:10:07,360
He'll be up soon, won't he?

127
00:10:07,734 --> 00:10:09,324
He's really going to be okay, right?

128
00:10:09,831 --> 00:10:11,037
Of course.

129
00:10:17,718 --> 00:10:19,844
You'll collapse yourself at this rate.

130
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:21,516
Aren't you dizzy?

131
00:10:21,851 --> 00:10:23,486
Want some water?

132
00:10:23,763 --> 00:10:27,942
Come on now, stop crying.

133
00:11:01,708 --> 00:11:03,177
Do you live around here?

134
00:11:03,202 --> 00:11:05,408
No. I mean, yes.

135
00:11:07,943 --> 00:11:09,818
People are going to think
we're a real couple.

136
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:11,738
I know.

137
00:11:12,759 --> 00:11:16,705
I'm confessing to you right now.

138
00:11:16,828 --> 00:11:19,179
Just look at me.

139
00:11:19,256 --> 00:11:21,422
I think I've fallen for you, Gyu Rim.

140
00:11:22,036 --> 00:11:25,018
If I don't tell you how I feel now,

141
00:11:25,687 --> 00:11:27,459
I felt like I'd lose you for good.

142
00:11:27,546 --> 00:11:28,951
My heart's pounding right now.

143
00:11:29,044 --> 00:11:32,564
This took real courage.

144
00:11:33,316 --> 00:11:35,081
Just keep falling for me.

145
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:36,860
Hide it if you like,

146
00:11:38,803 --> 00:11:40,178
but I'd rather you didn't.

147
00:11:40,937 --> 00:11:42,540
Hell or high water,

148
00:11:43,055 --> 00:11:45,791
I'll go anywhere with you,

149
00:11:46,028 --> 00:11:47,650
so don't run from me.

150
00:11:47,976 --> 00:11:49,632
Gyu Rim,

151
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:51,538
may I hold you?

152
00:11:51,770 --> 00:11:53,808
Why would we ever break up?

153
00:11:53,903 --> 00:11:55,908
That won't happen
as long as you don't leave.

154
00:11:56,084 --> 00:11:58,948
I spent all day terrified...

155
00:11:58,973 --> 00:12:01,144
that you'd want to end it.
Do you know how scared I was?

156
00:12:54,178 --> 00:12:56,511
(Seizure Notice)

157
00:13:00,357 --> 00:13:01,963
You can't take that off.

158
00:13:05,383 --> 00:13:06,943
What is this, Gyu Rim?

159
00:13:06,977 --> 00:13:09,277
It means those things aren't ours anymore.

160
00:13:09,302 --> 00:13:12,309
There's one on my bed and desk too.

161
00:13:13,164 --> 00:13:16,743
I'll buy you a new bed and desk soon,
Gyu Seo.

162
00:13:52,470 --> 00:13:53,969
This is Han Gyu Rim.

163
00:13:57,317 --> 00:13:58,710
Just give me the hundred thousand.

164
00:14:04,937 --> 00:14:06,157
A hundred thousand dollars?

165
00:14:06,443 --> 00:14:09,022
A hundred thousand to walk away
from Mu Jin,

166
00:14:09,191 --> 00:14:11,158
sounds like a fair deal to me.

167
00:14:12,578 --> 00:14:14,248
A deal?

168
00:14:14,273 --> 00:14:15,869
Honestly,

169
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:18,401
when I heard Mu Jin was rich,

170
00:14:18,793 --> 00:14:21,631
I was shocked, but part of me
was absolutely thrilled.

171
00:14:23,117 --> 00:14:26,155
Was I becoming the Cinderella
I'd only seen in movies?

172
00:14:26,696 --> 00:14:29,813
I'd never have to grind through
this miserable life again.

173
00:14:30,504 --> 00:14:32,552
I was thrilled. I really was.

174
00:14:34,484 --> 00:14:38,344
But then he's thrown out
and hurt working construction.

175
00:14:38,411 --> 00:14:40,204
I thought, "Wait..."

176
00:14:41,144 --> 00:14:42,744
"This isn't right."

177
00:14:42,891 --> 00:14:44,510
The more I thought about it,

178
00:14:44,991 --> 00:14:46,237
the more unsettled I felt.

179
00:14:46,262 --> 00:14:49,209
Is that really what you have to say
after seeing him fight for his life?

180
00:14:49,877 --> 00:14:51,593
And whose fault is it?

181
00:14:51,704 --> 00:14:54,370
Who did he give up everything for?

182
00:14:54,395 --> 00:14:56,933
I never asked him to give up everything.

183
00:14:59,037 --> 00:15:01,024
Didn't you love him?

184
00:15:01,164 --> 00:15:02,530
I did.

185
00:15:03,544 --> 00:15:05,142
I did love him,

186
00:15:05,463 --> 00:15:09,178
but once I found out
what kind of family he came from...

187
00:15:09,604 --> 00:15:11,233
Kim Mu Jin, a broke day laborer,

188
00:15:11,235 --> 00:15:13,144
What's so attractive about him now?

189
00:15:13,169 --> 00:15:14,831
How can you say that?

190
00:15:14,864 --> 00:15:16,450
As things stand,

191
00:15:16,663 --> 00:15:20,503
I'd be carrying him alone,
without a cent of support from you.

192
00:15:20,797 --> 00:15:22,803
Honestly, I'm not up for it.

193
00:15:23,544 --> 00:15:25,324
We dated for only one year.

194
00:15:25,751 --> 00:15:27,604
It's not like we're married.

195
00:15:27,924 --> 00:15:30,444
I'm barely holding on as it is.

196
00:15:30,817 --> 00:15:34,843
How do I know how long
those injuries will drag on?

197
00:15:35,311 --> 00:15:37,797
I can't. I don't want to.

198
00:15:37,977 --> 00:15:40,690
Are you even human?

199
00:15:40,923 --> 00:15:42,090
Are you?

200
00:15:44,870 --> 00:15:47,551
And he gave up everything
for a girl like you...

201
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:58,072
I don't want to waste another word
on someone as shallow as you.

202
00:15:58,097 --> 00:15:59,514
Don't ever contact me again.

203
00:16:06,497 --> 00:16:07,663
What's this?

204
00:16:07,851 --> 00:16:09,173
A voice recorder.

205
00:16:10,274 --> 00:16:14,196
Play it for him when he wakes up.

206
00:16:16,195 --> 00:16:19,784
He isn't a man who gives up easily.

207
00:16:21,269 --> 00:16:23,803
It'll take this much to put an end to it.

208
00:16:24,477 --> 00:16:27,178
So you planned this from the start...

209
00:16:30,303 --> 00:16:33,323
I'm sorry for the trouble I've caused.

210
00:16:34,797 --> 00:16:35,875
What about...

211
00:16:36,762 --> 00:16:38,257
the hundred thousand?

212
00:16:39,924 --> 00:16:41,044
I don't need it.

213
00:16:53,217 --> 00:16:55,066
Are you all right?

214
00:16:55,541 --> 00:16:58,277
The doctor says apart from the fracture,
everything is normal.

215
00:16:58,351 --> 00:16:59,936
You don't need to worry too much.

216
00:17:02,811 --> 00:17:03,924
Give me my phone.

217
00:17:04,384 --> 00:17:06,374
Your phone? It wasn't there.

218
00:17:06,638 --> 00:17:07,911
Did you lose it?

219
00:17:10,909 --> 00:17:12,110
What happened?

220
00:17:13,843 --> 00:17:15,309
How long has it been since the accident?

221
00:17:15,717 --> 00:17:16,764
Three days.

222
00:17:18,677 --> 00:17:19,745
Gyu Rim...

223
00:17:20,606 --> 00:17:22,217
She must be worried sick.

224
00:17:23,151 --> 00:17:25,604
She came by.

225
00:17:26,564 --> 00:17:27,724
Did you tell her everything?

226
00:17:29,290 --> 00:17:31,258
Did you tell her I got hurt
on a construction site?

227
00:17:32,644 --> 00:17:34,264
I told her you were walking along...

228
00:17:35,211 --> 00:17:38,284
and lightning struck you out of the sky.

229
00:17:40,736 --> 00:17:41,771
Well,

230
00:17:42,379 --> 00:17:44,305
I made something up,
said I didn't really know either,

231
00:17:44,330 --> 00:17:46,083
that I got the call and rushed over.

232
00:17:47,730 --> 00:17:50,139
You're dead if you tell her the truth.

233
00:17:51,603 --> 00:17:53,449
Dead either way, I suppose.

234
00:17:54,011 --> 00:17:55,874
- What?
- Nothing.

235
00:17:57,450 --> 00:17:59,317
Gyu Rim must be worried a lot, right?

236
00:18:02,744 --> 00:18:03,865
Well...

237
00:18:04,932 --> 00:18:07,036
She came the first day
and never came back.

238
00:18:07,184 --> 00:18:09,717
Not one call to ask how you were.

239
00:18:14,498 --> 00:18:16,571
What are you doing?
Going to her in that state?

240
00:18:17,910 --> 00:18:19,431
Call Gyu Rim for me.

241
00:18:28,045 --> 00:18:29,931
The number you have dialed
is unavailable...

242
00:18:29,956 --> 00:18:31,523
No answer. She must be busy.

243
00:18:31,590 --> 00:18:33,114
Try once more.

244
00:18:44,449 --> 00:18:45,718
The number you have dialed...

245
00:18:45,743 --> 00:18:46,840
She's not picking up.

246
00:18:46,983 --> 00:18:49,597
Text her that I'm awake,

247
00:18:49,805 --> 00:18:51,823
and that she shouldn't worry.

248
00:18:52,137 --> 00:18:53,150
All right.

249
00:18:54,031 --> 00:18:56,504
Jeong Woo, could you give us a moment?

250
00:18:56,884 --> 00:18:58,350
- Sure.
- Thanks.

251
00:19:05,072 --> 00:19:08,257
- You all right?
- I'm fine.

252
00:19:08,746 --> 00:19:10,170
Sorry for scaring you.

253
00:19:11,563 --> 00:19:13,264
There's something I need to tell you.

254
00:19:13,883 --> 00:19:17,586
I thought about waiting
until you'd recovered,

255
00:19:18,469 --> 00:19:21,173
- but it's better you hear it now.
- What is it?

256
00:19:21,349 --> 00:19:24,621
About the Han Gyu Rim
you gave up everything for.

257
00:19:25,717 --> 00:19:26,900
You met her?

258
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:29,190
She called and asked to meet.

259
00:19:38,003 --> 00:19:39,222
Just give me the hundred thousand.

260
00:19:40,650 --> 00:19:41,751
A hundred thousand dollars?

261
00:19:42,763 --> 00:19:46,992
A hundred thousand to walk away
from Mu Jin sounds like a fair deal.

262
00:19:48,336 --> 00:19:50,824
(Seizure Notice)

263
00:19:50,937 --> 00:19:52,227
Honestly,

264
00:19:52,795 --> 00:19:55,131
when I heard Mu Jin was rich,

265
00:19:55,348 --> 00:19:58,472
I was shocked, but part of me
was absolutely thrilled.

266
00:19:59,724 --> 00:20:02,708
Was I becoming the Cinderella
I'd only seen in movies?

267
00:20:03,417 --> 00:20:06,697
I'd never have to grind through
this miserable life again.

268
00:20:07,264 --> 00:20:09,267
I was thrilled. I really was.

269
00:20:10,063 --> 00:20:11,644
As things stand,

270
00:20:11,950 --> 00:20:15,861
I'd be carrying him alone,
without a cent of support from you.

271
00:20:16,137 --> 00:20:17,928
Honestly, I'm not up for it.

272
00:20:18,036 --> 00:20:19,610
We dated for one year,

273
00:20:20,197 --> 00:20:21,910
it's not like we're married,

274
00:20:22,423 --> 00:20:24,723
and I'm barely holding on as it is.

275
00:20:24,970 --> 00:20:28,909
How do I know how long
those injuries will drag on?

276
00:20:29,443 --> 00:20:30,593
I can't do it.

277
00:20:30,734 --> 00:20:33,074
- I don't want to.
- Turn it off.

278
00:20:38,164 --> 00:20:40,268
What did you do to Gyu Rim?

279
00:20:42,457 --> 00:20:45,744
What would I have to do
to make her say things like that?

280
00:20:53,870 --> 00:20:55,485
I want to be alone.

281
00:21:00,037 --> 00:21:02,657
All right. Get some rest.

282
00:21:30,343 --> 00:21:32,252
Thank you. I've had a look around.

283
00:21:32,837 --> 00:21:34,845
- All right, goodbye.
- Thank you.

284
00:22:49,633 --> 00:22:51,427
- You okay?
- Yes.

285
00:23:09,581 --> 00:23:10,994
Thanks.

286
00:23:32,171 --> 00:23:33,401
Who are you?

287
00:23:39,504 --> 00:23:40,750
Is Gyu Rim here?

288
00:23:40,976 --> 00:23:41,989
Who?

289
00:23:43,450 --> 00:23:44,463
Han Gyu Rim.

290
00:23:45,231 --> 00:23:46,850
Did you just come out of the house?

291
00:23:47,017 --> 00:23:50,289
What are you talking about?
It's my house. I live here.

292
00:23:52,036 --> 00:23:53,339
So you've just moved in...

293
00:23:53,798 --> 00:23:54,809
Then...

294
00:23:55,416 --> 00:23:59,138
- what about the people who lived here...
- How would I know?

295
00:23:59,464 --> 00:24:00,844
The people who lived here...

296
00:24:00,869 --> 00:24:02,493
even after they got an eviction order,

297
00:24:02,518 --> 00:24:05,651
they took forever to move out.
They were such a nightmare.

298
00:24:18,902 --> 00:24:21,642
(Gyu Rim)

299
00:24:23,363 --> 00:24:26,210
The number you have dialed
is not in service.

300
00:24:26,377 --> 00:24:28,780
Please check the number and try again.

301
00:25:17,151 --> 00:25:21,665
(Eight years later)

302
00:25:21,708 --> 00:25:23,646
(The Most Precious Thing in the World)

303
00:25:31,524 --> 00:25:34,098
Is that a flower?

304
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:38,222
And what's this puppy?

305
00:25:38,739 --> 00:25:40,784
- Is that your puppy, Yun Hu?
- Yes.

306
00:25:41,063 --> 00:25:42,751
So cute.

307
00:25:42,937 --> 00:25:45,199
- Isn't he pretty?
- Yes, very pretty.

308
00:25:49,130 --> 00:25:51,357
- Is that your teddy bear, Jin Ju?
- Yes.

309
00:25:51,604 --> 00:25:54,703
It must be your favorite bear.
Five hearts.

310
00:25:58,996 --> 00:26:01,332
You drew it so well.

311
00:26:01,638 --> 00:26:05,477
Who's this? The most precious person
in the world to you, Gyeol?

312
00:26:05,502 --> 00:26:06,721
That's my mom.

313
00:26:07,230 --> 00:26:09,926
Your mom must be so happy.

314
00:26:13,111 --> 00:26:17,414
But Gyeol, what's this dot?

315
00:26:18,097 --> 00:26:19,356
That's my dad.

316
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:23,414
- Your dad?
- Yes.

317
00:26:24,110 --> 00:26:25,855
But he's still precious to you, right?

318
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:27,720
You did draw him, even as a dot.

319
00:26:27,985 --> 00:26:30,892
Well, he did bring me into the world.

320
00:26:31,063 --> 00:26:33,023
That's about how grateful I am.

321
00:26:34,373 --> 00:26:35,464
I see.

322
00:26:37,855 --> 00:26:40,064
Mom!

323
00:26:43,317 --> 00:26:46,171
- My boy! You're back?
- Mom!

324
00:26:47,832 --> 00:26:50,064
How was school? Did you have fun?

325
00:26:50,066 --> 00:26:52,457
Yes, it was fun. This is for you.

326
00:26:52,916 --> 00:26:54,086
What's this?

327
00:26:57,329 --> 00:27:00,275
Gyeol, who's this pretty lady?

328
00:27:00,844 --> 00:27:01,940
That's you.

329
00:27:01,994 --> 00:27:05,070
My teacher told us to draw
the most precious thing in the world.

330
00:27:06,263 --> 00:27:09,583
- I'm the most precious person to you?
- Yes.

331
00:27:09,965 --> 00:27:13,163
And next week I'm representing
my class in the art contest.

332
00:27:13,370 --> 00:27:15,910
Really? You're the best, Gyeol!

333
00:27:16,236 --> 00:27:17,473
Yes!

334
00:27:17,904 --> 00:27:19,702
You must be so pleased.

335
00:27:19,757 --> 00:27:23,350
A sweet, pretty daughter-in-law
and a bright, adorable grandson.

336
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:27,564
Of course I am. Couldn't be happier.

337
00:27:27,617 --> 00:27:29,683
Why am I your grandson?

338
00:27:30,184 --> 00:27:32,735
And why is my mom your daughter-in-law?

339
00:27:32,737 --> 00:27:34,083
Why are you making things up?

340
00:27:34,377 --> 00:27:36,963
I'm saying I think of you and your mom...

341
00:27:37,009 --> 00:27:40,392
as my grandson and daughter-in-law.

342
00:27:40,975 --> 00:27:44,011
How can something so tiny be so prickly?

343
00:27:44,891 --> 00:27:48,074
- Good luck with sales.
- Enjoy it and come again.

344
00:27:48,454 --> 00:27:49,970
Goodbye.

345
00:27:50,176 --> 00:27:53,551
Now, come on,

346
00:27:53,816 --> 00:27:56,374
we've spent enough years together,

347
00:27:56,684 --> 00:28:00,010
so let's make it official already.

348
00:28:00,035 --> 00:28:01,041
No.

349
00:28:02,824 --> 00:28:06,197
Gyeol, are you going to keep
being rude to Su Nam?

350
00:28:06,230 --> 00:28:11,090
But what if her tall tales
keep you from getting married?

351
00:28:12,096 --> 00:28:13,556
Why wouldn't she get married?

352
00:28:13,558 --> 00:28:16,031
Heung Sik is right there waiting.

353
00:28:16,033 --> 00:28:18,203
Exactly. That's the problem.

354
00:28:18,978 --> 00:28:20,696
What on earth is that supposed to mean?

355
00:28:21,004 --> 00:28:23,430
What's the problem with my son waiting?

356
00:28:23,432 --> 00:28:25,671
Let's leave it there and get to work.

357
00:28:26,411 --> 00:28:30,157
You just don't know any better.
In all the world,

358
00:28:30,270 --> 00:28:32,837
there's no better man than my son.

359
00:28:33,717 --> 00:28:36,157
Still, my mom's too good for him.

360
00:28:36,331 --> 00:28:39,004
Even if Kim Woo Bin came along,
she'd still be too good for him.

361
00:28:39,484 --> 00:28:41,229
What am I to do with you?

362
00:28:41,231 --> 00:28:45,577
So little and so picky
when you know nothing.

363
00:28:49,742 --> 00:28:51,744
Gyeol, check my phone for me.

364
00:28:57,132 --> 00:28:59,132
(Gyu Yeong)

365
00:29:00,017 --> 00:29:02,891
- It's Gyu Yeong.
- Could you take it?

366
00:29:07,051 --> 00:29:10,011
Hey, you know that white dress
I bought last month?

367
00:29:10,090 --> 00:29:12,644
The chiffon one, all floaty.

368
00:29:12,987 --> 00:29:15,334
I need it tomorrow,
so take it to the cleaners...

369
00:29:15,359 --> 00:29:16,971
Is my mom your secretary?

370
00:29:17,151 --> 00:29:19,071
Do your own errands.

371
00:29:19,096 --> 00:29:21,009
Stop working my mom to the bone!

372
00:29:22,537 --> 00:29:23,551
Hey.

373
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:26,955
Gyeol...

374
00:29:27,916 --> 00:29:30,883
Good for you. Well done, Gyeol.

375
00:29:31,437 --> 00:29:36,723
I feel like a huge weight
has finally been lifted.

376
00:29:37,203 --> 00:29:41,011
Your aunt, that sly woman,
needed to be put in her place.

377
00:29:41,697 --> 00:29:45,231
Well done, sharp one.

378
00:29:51,010 --> 00:29:52,397
That little thing!

379
00:30:00,124 --> 00:30:01,727
Yes, sweetheart.

380
00:30:01,752 --> 00:30:02,854
(Medical License)

381
00:30:02,879 --> 00:30:05,847
I wanted to wear it tomorrow
to your cousin's wedding,

382
00:30:05,895 --> 00:30:08,117
so I asked my sister
to take it to the cleaners,

383
00:30:08,443 --> 00:30:09,993
but that little squirt Gyeol,

384
00:30:10,820 --> 00:30:12,777
told me not to work his mom...

385
00:30:16,930 --> 00:30:18,000
Really?

386
00:30:18,206 --> 00:30:20,750
I was just upset, that's all...

387
00:30:21,417 --> 00:30:23,417
You'll really buy me a new dress?

388
00:30:23,897 --> 00:30:26,743
You're the absolute best.

389
00:30:27,792 --> 00:30:29,197
Yes.

390
00:30:30,131 --> 00:30:31,850
(Cliad Medical Skin Clinic)

391
00:30:31,852 --> 00:30:34,631
It's time for Song Ji Yeong's
consultation.

392
00:30:34,704 --> 00:30:37,487
- Send her in.
- Yes.

393
00:30:39,436 --> 00:30:42,758
I'll see you after work, sweetheart.

394
00:30:42,783 --> 00:30:44,132
Sure.

395
00:30:48,806 --> 00:30:50,489
(Doctor Han Gyu Yeong)

396
00:30:54,771 --> 00:30:56,344
What brings you in today?

397
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:58,220
Could I...

398
00:30:59,063 --> 00:31:01,437
look like Suzy too?

399
00:31:02,684 --> 00:31:05,863
- Sorry? Suzy?
- Yes.

400
00:31:08,384 --> 00:31:11,451
It's not possible, is it?

401
00:31:12,857 --> 00:31:14,187
Absolutely not.

402
00:31:14,211 --> 00:31:16,997
You'd struggle even if you died
and tried again in the next life.

403
00:31:20,220 --> 00:31:21,803
(Clinic Revenue equals Incentives)

404
00:31:24,504 --> 00:31:26,719
It won't be easy, of course,

405
00:31:26,721 --> 00:31:28,557
but nothing is impossible.

406
00:31:28,744 --> 00:31:31,897
Shall we find a way together,
step by step?

407
00:31:31,922 --> 00:31:32,942
Yes.

408
00:31:52,711 --> 00:31:54,757
Excuse me, how about getting up?

409
00:31:55,224 --> 00:31:57,131
It's past three in the afternoon.

410
00:32:00,364 --> 00:32:02,224
If you were asleep when I left for school,

411
00:32:02,538 --> 00:32:04,084
shouldn't you at least be awake...

412
00:32:04,578 --> 00:32:06,544
by the time I get back?

413
00:32:13,397 --> 00:32:15,637
How long do you plan to live like this?

414
00:32:16,171 --> 00:32:18,351
You've got your whole life ahead of you.

415
00:32:18,412 --> 00:32:21,324
Don't you want to start living
properly, even now?

416
00:32:22,501 --> 00:32:24,564
You sound just like an old lady...

417
00:32:25,097 --> 00:32:27,250
Why do you talk like that? It's so weird.

418
00:32:27,371 --> 00:32:30,522
Don't change the subject.
Are you going to sort yourself out or not?

419
00:32:30,524 --> 00:32:33,335
Why do you care
whether I get my act together or not?

420
00:32:33,336 --> 00:32:36,476
Because if you don't,
my mom has to work harder.

421
00:32:36,950 --> 00:32:38,159
What a devoted son.

422
00:32:38,257 --> 00:32:40,187
Makes those of us without sons jealous.

423
00:32:45,824 --> 00:32:46,833
Listen, Gyeol.

424
00:32:47,254 --> 00:32:48,979
Like I always say,

425
00:32:48,981 --> 00:32:51,212
my life is mine, and yours is yours.

426
00:32:51,563 --> 00:32:54,132
From now on, let's stay out
of each other's lives.

427
00:32:55,228 --> 00:32:58,464
- Deal?
- We're not strangers. We're family.

428
00:32:58,524 --> 00:33:00,399
How can family do that?

429
00:33:18,657 --> 00:33:22,437
Look at that cool expression. I can't!

430
00:33:22,518 --> 00:33:23,609
I'm dying.

431
00:33:23,697 --> 00:33:26,191
If what I'm looking
at isn't perfection, then what is?

432
00:33:26,257 --> 00:33:30,094
When Gyu Seo graduates next year,
I might just drop out.

433
00:33:30,364 --> 00:33:33,689
There's no point being here without him.

434
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:35,908
- He's so handsome.
- Ridiculously handsome.

435
00:33:35,933 --> 00:33:37,580
Can I have one of these?

436
00:33:38,404 --> 00:33:39,537
Can I have one too?

437
00:33:39,539 --> 00:33:40,895
- Sure.
- Thanks.

438
00:33:41,369 --> 00:33:44,647
- Idol trainees really are different.
- Seriously.

439
00:33:46,496 --> 00:33:49,443
This is some serious relative deprivation.

440
00:33:49,656 --> 00:33:52,271
Is it really relative?
Feels pretty absolute.

441
00:33:52,296 --> 00:33:54,388
- Let's play football.
- At lunch, yeah.

442
00:33:54,413 --> 00:33:58,340
Hey, I heard his twin sister
goes here too.

443
00:33:58,477 --> 00:34:01,122
If she's his twin,
she must be gorgeous, right?

444
00:34:01,906 --> 00:34:03,300
You idiot.

445
00:34:03,414 --> 00:34:08,057
Did you forget last year, when you begged
to switch seats because you hated her?

446
00:34:08,059 --> 00:34:10,017
Why bring her up and jinx the day?

447
00:34:10,019 --> 00:34:11,857
- Okay.
- Want to join us?

448
00:34:12,471 --> 00:34:13,930
He and she are twins?

449
00:34:14,204 --> 00:34:15,224
I should make friends.

450
00:34:16,400 --> 00:34:17,436
Unbelievable...

451
00:34:17,529 --> 00:34:18,837
There's some left, though.

452
00:34:18,839 --> 00:34:21,750
Gyu Min. Han Gyu Min.

453
00:34:22,577 --> 00:34:25,701
Set me up with Gyu Seo just once.

454
00:34:25,968 --> 00:34:27,655
Please.

455
00:34:28,697 --> 00:34:30,377
You like spicy rice cakes, right?

456
00:34:30,510 --> 00:34:32,580
I'll treat you to the best place around,

457
00:34:32,676 --> 00:34:34,043
so how about you bring Gyu Seo along?

458
00:34:34,557 --> 00:34:36,717
Or just invite me to your place once?

459
00:34:37,104 --> 00:34:38,393
When's your birthday?

460
00:34:38,457 --> 00:34:41,664
You're twins, so September 10, right?

461
00:34:43,980 --> 00:34:46,704
I'm not close with Han Gyu Seo.

462
00:34:46,706 --> 00:34:50,044
If you want to meet him,
go talk to him yourselves,

463
00:34:50,650 --> 00:34:52,046
and take all of this back.

464
00:34:52,154 --> 00:34:54,191
Gyu Min.

465
00:34:54,636 --> 00:34:56,065
I'm going home.

466
00:34:56,571 --> 00:34:59,101
Han Gyu Min! Let's go home.

467
00:35:06,197 --> 00:35:08,548
Where are you going?

468
00:35:11,310 --> 00:35:13,017
- Han Gyu Seo!
- Su Bin.

469
00:35:13,019 --> 00:35:14,908
- What?
- I'm off.

470
00:35:14,910 --> 00:35:17,177
- Go ahead.
- Han Gyu Min, wait for me.

471
00:35:19,190 --> 00:35:20,721
Get off me, Han Gyu Seo.

472
00:35:21,229 --> 00:35:23,851
I'm begging you,
stop acting like we're close.

473
00:35:23,876 --> 00:35:26,502
How am I supposed to act?

474
00:35:27,190 --> 00:35:29,830
- We are close.
- Hey.

475
00:35:30,671 --> 00:35:32,653
We're family, and twins on top of that,

476
00:35:32,954 --> 00:35:35,370
so it'd be stranger to act like we're not.

477
00:35:36,711 --> 00:35:39,008
Do you know how much grief you cause me?

478
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:41,851
Because of you, I have no life at all.
None.

479
00:35:42,351 --> 00:35:43,480
All I want...

480
00:35:43,641 --> 00:35:46,370
is to keep my head down and go unnoticed.

481
00:35:46,777 --> 00:35:50,470
At school at least,
can we be strangers? Please.

482
00:35:51,390 --> 00:35:53,437
Fine, I get it. I'm sorry.

483
00:35:56,618 --> 00:35:57,795
But you're not...

484
00:35:58,842 --> 00:36:00,404
sulking, are you?

485
00:36:07,173 --> 00:36:10,333
You scared me. Don't do that.

486
00:36:10,844 --> 00:36:12,679
We're outside the gates,
so this isn't school.

487
00:36:12,704 --> 00:36:14,370
Inside, I'll do as you say,

488
00:36:14,474 --> 00:36:16,897
so outside I get to do as I please, right?

489
00:36:17,984 --> 00:36:19,399
So now you're acting close?

490
00:36:19,763 --> 00:36:22,625
You know you're the worst?

491
00:36:22,817 --> 00:36:24,411
I suppose I am.

492
00:36:26,369 --> 00:36:29,085
- Why take my bag?
- Heavy bags stunt your growth.

493
00:36:29,255 --> 00:36:32,081
Let's squeeze out every last inch
while you still can.

494
00:36:33,704 --> 00:36:37,170
Get over here. Give it back. Give it.

495
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:39,491
Grow up big and strong
and enter a beauty pageant.

496
00:36:39,666 --> 00:36:42,306
You should've shared some of that height!

497
00:36:42,474 --> 00:36:43,788
Still angry?

498
00:36:44,377 --> 00:36:46,441
Want spicy rice cakes? My treat.

499
00:36:46,521 --> 00:36:48,286
No, you go ahead and eat.

500
00:36:48,311 --> 00:36:50,257
They're terrible for a diet.

501
00:36:50,891 --> 00:36:52,247
You're not on a diet, are you?

502
00:36:52,871 --> 00:36:54,424
You were wolfing down
black bean noodles yesterday,

503
00:36:54,449 --> 00:36:56,097
so I figured the diet was over.

504
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:59,381
I am on one. The weight just won't go.

505
00:36:59,861 --> 00:37:01,545
And the black bean noodles were your idea.

506
00:37:02,205 --> 00:37:04,024
Han Gyu Seo, hey.

507
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:07,390
Who are you?

508
00:37:08,154 --> 00:37:10,314
Why have you been trailing us for days?

509
00:37:14,171 --> 00:37:17,646
Are you the woman who abandoned us?

510
00:37:18,551 --> 00:37:21,903
The gold digger who ran off in the night
with another man and everything we had?

511
00:37:25,931 --> 00:37:27,194
Ma'am!

512
00:37:30,567 --> 00:37:32,735
I'm sorry for following you.

513
00:37:33,135 --> 00:37:37,333
My daughter's completely lovesick
over you,

514
00:37:37,796 --> 00:37:43,561
so I came to see
just how handsome you are.

515
00:37:44,647 --> 00:37:46,024
Honestly,

516
00:37:46,271 --> 00:37:49,972
Why do you have to look
like an idol and draw a crowd?

517
00:37:50,339 --> 00:37:52,273
Just debut already.

518
00:37:52,357 --> 00:37:54,587
Then we could watch you from home on TV.

519
00:37:55,316 --> 00:37:56,748
My arm.

520
00:38:06,150 --> 00:38:07,333
Let's go.

521
00:38:09,991 --> 00:38:11,249
(No couples allowed)

522
00:38:11,271 --> 00:38:13,864
(Da Solo welcomes solo diners,
friends, and family gatherings)

523
00:38:23,354 --> 00:38:26,117
One T-bone and one tomato pasta
for table three.

524
00:38:26,155 --> 00:38:27,488
Yes, Chef.

525
00:38:31,201 --> 00:38:32,478
When did you make this?

526
00:38:32,984 --> 00:38:34,284
An hour ago.

527
00:38:34,887 --> 00:38:36,227
It's fine.

528
00:38:40,970 --> 00:38:42,677
- A little less salt too.
- Yes.

529
00:38:46,798 --> 00:38:48,096
You'll break the grains that way.

530
00:38:48,121 --> 00:38:50,152
- Fold it in, like this.
- Yes, Chef.

531
00:39:18,331 --> 00:39:21,789
Everyone, this place lives up to the hype.

532
00:39:21,814 --> 00:39:24,217
The taste goes without saying.

533
00:39:24,340 --> 00:39:29,216
Can you see the quality
of every single ingredient?

534
00:39:29,363 --> 00:39:32,097
It's absolutely superb.

535
00:39:32,351 --> 00:39:34,458
First, the vegetables,

536
00:39:34,617 --> 00:39:37,511
so crisp and fresh you'd think
they were picked minutes ago.

537
00:39:37,578 --> 00:39:41,206
The meat has flavor, juices, and a sear
with nothing missing.

538
00:39:41,531 --> 00:39:42,758
But,

539
00:39:43,102 --> 00:39:46,911
this place isn't just famous for the food.

540
00:39:48,709 --> 00:39:53,207
Right. Is this really a paradise
for singles and doom for couples?

541
00:39:53,291 --> 00:39:55,555
Couples who aren't on a family register,

542
00:39:55,645 --> 00:39:59,741
guy friends, girl friends,
men, women, all of them.

543
00:39:59,978 --> 00:40:01,125
Anyway,

544
00:40:01,511 --> 00:40:03,004
are all couples really banned...

545
00:40:03,029 --> 00:40:04,304
from entering and dining?

546
00:40:04,537 --> 00:40:06,503
That's what's left to confirm.

547
00:40:09,363 --> 00:40:12,867
They look ordinary at first glance.

548
00:40:13,699 --> 00:40:17,453
All family? Or married?

549
00:40:17,770 --> 00:40:18,876
By any chance,

550
00:40:21,311 --> 00:40:22,624
are you really married?

551
00:40:23,135 --> 00:40:24,441
Aren't you high schoolers?

552
00:40:25,518 --> 00:40:28,160
Of course we are. We just look young.

553
00:40:30,542 --> 00:40:31,779
May I see
your family relations certificate?

554
00:40:32,213 --> 00:40:35,024
I forgot to bring it.

555
00:40:35,952 --> 00:40:37,657
You can pull it up
on your phone these days.

556
00:40:37,682 --> 00:40:39,391
Just access the government portal...

557
00:40:39,460 --> 00:40:43,672
What restaurant asks customers
for a family relationship certificate?

558
00:40:44,171 --> 00:40:47,102
Can you really demand
people's personal information?

559
00:40:47,127 --> 00:40:51,154
That was the rule from the start.
If you don't like it, go elsewhere.

560
00:40:52,067 --> 00:40:54,701
We won't charge you for the meal,
so please leave.

561
00:40:56,293 --> 00:40:58,024
Let's go, honey.

562
00:41:06,670 --> 00:41:07,963
Would you clear this away?

563
00:41:09,949 --> 00:41:12,179
Chef, we need to talk.

564
00:41:13,750 --> 00:41:14,862
Go ahead.

565
00:41:29,411 --> 00:41:30,564
You absolute...

566
00:41:31,485 --> 00:41:32,752
lunatic.

567
00:41:32,904 --> 00:41:37,031
Of all people to fight, a customer,
and over something that ridiculous.

568
00:41:37,230 --> 00:41:38,430
Ridiculous?

569
00:41:39,097 --> 00:41:41,268
You said it sounded fun when we opened.

570
00:41:41,590 --> 00:41:43,328
What exactly is the problem?

571
00:41:46,237 --> 00:41:49,181
The fact that you can't see the problem
is the problem.

572
00:41:49,871 --> 00:41:51,591
Why should your absurd rule...

573
00:41:51,607 --> 00:41:54,421
force perfectly happy couples
to take separate tables,

574
00:41:54,441 --> 00:41:55,824
sit apart,

575
00:41:56,188 --> 00:41:58,591
pining over Wi-Fi like separated lovers,

576
00:41:58,624 --> 00:42:01,289
then reunite outside
like long-lost family?

577
00:42:01,653 --> 00:42:04,432
Who are you to tear couples apart?

578
00:42:04,457 --> 00:42:06,623
What are you, some kind
of relationship wrecker?

579
00:42:07,476 --> 00:42:09,426
If they don't like it,
they can eat somewhere else.

580
00:42:09,451 --> 00:42:11,024
Running a charity, are we?

581
00:42:11,741 --> 00:42:14,918
What, are you keeping every other
restaurant around here in business?

582
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:17,202
Ever since we opened,
business has been dead...

583
00:42:17,555 --> 00:42:21,335
every Valentine's Day, White Day,
and Christmas have been a bust.

584
00:42:22,524 --> 00:42:25,117
Whenever everyone else is cashing in,

585
00:42:25,161 --> 00:42:27,296
you always have to make things
worse for me.

586
00:42:27,321 --> 00:42:28,976
This is all because of Han Gyu Rim...

587
00:42:33,627 --> 00:42:34,943
Fighting again?

588
00:42:35,514 --> 00:42:38,697
Your ages add up to 70 now.
Aren't you embarrassed?

589
00:42:39,122 --> 00:42:40,465
Good timing, Seo Hyeon.

590
00:42:41,531 --> 00:42:43,331
Listen and judge for yourself.

591
00:42:43,871 --> 00:42:49,500
Is it sane to run a restaurant
and turn couples away like this?

592
00:42:52,391 --> 00:42:54,613
Some customers will take offense.

593
00:42:54,764 --> 00:42:58,865
But you said plenty come
precisely because it's fun.

594
00:42:59,114 --> 00:43:01,144
You said single people call the place
their own personal paradise,

595
00:43:01,169 --> 00:43:03,024
and back it wholeheartedly.

596
00:43:03,334 --> 00:43:04,812
Right, Jang Seo Hyeon.

597
00:43:05,012 --> 00:43:08,235
You'd take his side
even if he sold the country out.

598
00:43:08,963 --> 00:43:11,056
I was an idiot to ask you.

599
00:43:11,321 --> 00:43:12,470
I'm off.

600
00:43:12,611 --> 00:43:14,411
I'm not finished. Where are you going?

601
00:43:15,758 --> 00:43:17,024
Honestly,

602
00:43:17,095 --> 00:43:20,666
I don't know why we have to fight
this hard over this,

603
00:43:21,194 --> 00:43:24,048
but if it's stressing you out that much,
I'll give it another thought.

604
00:43:24,152 --> 00:43:25,608
Let's talk again before we open tomorrow.

605
00:43:25,633 --> 00:43:28,128
At this rate, we'll just end up
sniping at each other.

606
00:43:36,171 --> 00:43:37,561
Doesn't it get old?

607
00:43:39,089 --> 00:43:40,293
What?

608
00:43:40,650 --> 00:43:44,815
Staring at the back of a man's head
when he won't even look at you.

609
00:43:46,811 --> 00:43:48,736
I've seen it so much I'm used to it now.

610
00:43:49,514 --> 00:43:52,857
You're not getting any younger.
How long are you...

611
00:43:52,882 --> 00:43:54,663
Until I'm 40.

612
00:43:55,184 --> 00:43:56,650
Doing what until you're 40?

613
00:43:57,214 --> 00:44:01,000
I've liked him since I was ten.
That's 30 years by the time I'm 40.

614
00:44:02,061 --> 00:44:04,445
If it's still not meant to be,
I'll give up.

615
00:44:08,023 --> 00:44:09,894
Found something to tease me about again.

616
00:44:10,091 --> 00:44:12,024
On your 30th anniversary
of unrequited love,

617
00:44:12,077 --> 00:44:15,644
win or lose, I'll hang
a gold medal around your neck.

618
00:44:15,731 --> 00:44:18,824
Thirty years at anything...

619
00:44:19,078 --> 00:44:22,450
deserves that much praise and respect.

620
00:44:23,531 --> 00:44:27,801
If you're giving one, make it solid gold.
Chain and medal both.

621
00:44:27,851 --> 00:44:30,011
A full 30 grams.

622
00:44:30,036 --> 00:44:34,146
Are you insane?
Do you know the price of gold now?

623
00:44:38,539 --> 00:44:41,379
Jeong Woo, I'm off. See you.

624
00:44:46,272 --> 00:44:47,792
She's not right in the head either.

625
00:44:48,797 --> 00:44:49,995
Mu Jin.

626
00:44:53,531 --> 00:44:54,874
Where are you going?

627
00:44:55,788 --> 00:44:57,857
I've got something on.

628
00:45:00,163 --> 00:45:01,489
Let's eat together another time.

629
00:45:01,514 --> 00:45:02,790
Where to?

630
00:45:03,607 --> 00:45:04,967
Meeting a woman?

631
00:45:05,591 --> 00:45:06,759
It's nothing like that.

632
00:45:06,884 --> 00:45:07,891
Then I'll come along.

633
00:45:07,916 --> 00:45:09,166
That settles it.

634
00:45:10,230 --> 00:45:11,481
Hey.

635
00:45:25,511 --> 00:45:26,783
Got you.

636
00:45:33,500 --> 00:45:34,595
So close.

637
00:45:36,353 --> 00:45:38,411
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

638
00:45:39,024 --> 00:45:40,421
What's this, a corn dog?

639
00:45:40,864 --> 00:45:42,296
Is a corn dog going to be enough?

640
00:45:43,585 --> 00:45:45,404
Eat, do what you need to,
and head off first.

641
00:45:45,502 --> 00:45:48,130
It's fine. I have emails to send,

642
00:45:48,251 --> 00:45:49,986
so don't mind me
and do what you came to do.

643
00:45:50,011 --> 00:45:52,601
Yeah? All right.

644
00:45:55,357 --> 00:45:57,101
One more round.

645
00:45:58,803 --> 00:46:01,116
(Tyrant of Steel)

646
00:46:01,141 --> 00:46:02,589
Got him!

647
00:46:06,407 --> 00:46:08,533
How does a person change this much?

648
00:46:09,783 --> 00:46:11,743
There we go. Dodged it.

649
00:46:14,234 --> 00:46:15,931
Did he really hit his head that hard?

650
00:46:28,588 --> 00:46:30,932
I just got him, right?

651
00:46:33,203 --> 00:46:34,521
Come on.

652
00:46:37,944 --> 00:46:40,671
You're that mad about coming in fourth?

653
00:46:40,748 --> 00:46:42,376
Come on!

654
00:46:42,401 --> 00:46:44,341
What's wrong?

655
00:46:44,377 --> 00:46:47,721
This guy keeps blocking me
and blasting me with items.

656
00:46:47,857 --> 00:46:48,990
What?

657
00:46:49,649 --> 00:46:51,621
He did this last time too.

658
00:46:52,001 --> 00:46:55,320
I'd worn the boss down, and he swooped
in for the final hit and stole the kill,

659
00:46:55,384 --> 00:46:58,005
took all the points and leveled up.
Where does that leave me?

660
00:46:58,558 --> 00:47:00,862
That's such a dirty way to play.

661
00:47:00,917 --> 00:47:03,262
What a no-life loser.

662
00:47:04,314 --> 00:47:05,708
This is pissing me off.

663
00:47:06,622 --> 00:47:07,851
Hey there.

664
00:47:08,647 --> 00:47:10,247
- Hey, what are you doing?
- What?

665
00:47:10,702 --> 00:47:12,608
You keep getting in my way.

666
00:47:12,869 --> 00:47:14,416
You did the same thing
when I was fighting the boss.

667
00:47:14,474 --> 00:47:17,451
I didn't know. Sorry. It was an accident.

668
00:47:19,857 --> 00:47:21,783
Didn't know? Accident?

669
00:47:22,276 --> 00:47:24,916
If you're that clueless
you must be a beginner,

670
00:47:24,941 --> 00:47:26,624
then stick to your own level.

671
00:47:26,857 --> 00:47:28,894
Seriously, quit playing like that.

672
00:47:28,923 --> 00:47:32,504
Excuse me. It was an accident
and I already apologized for it.

673
00:47:32,646 --> 00:47:34,286
That's uncalled for.

674
00:47:37,217 --> 00:47:39,989
So what you did doesn't matter,
but what I said does?

675
00:47:40,304 --> 00:47:43,870
You mess someone up on purpose,
then "sorry, accident" and that's it?

676
00:47:44,057 --> 00:47:48,244
Jeong Woo was right.
People really turn into kids over games.

677
00:47:48,504 --> 00:47:51,385
People like this need to be called out.

678
00:47:54,783 --> 00:47:57,575
(It's just a game. Why so serious...)

679
00:47:59,295 --> 00:48:02,386
Seriously. What is wrong with you?

680
00:48:02,411 --> 00:48:03,813
You want some?

681
00:48:05,821 --> 00:48:07,934
Why do you always say stuff like that?

682
00:48:08,280 --> 00:48:09,598
I swear.

683
00:48:12,112 --> 00:48:13,329
Mom!

684
00:48:13,719 --> 00:48:18,088
How dare you threaten
somebody's precious son?

685
00:48:19,257 --> 00:48:21,411
Move aside, Gyeol. Move.

686
00:48:21,843 --> 00:48:22,957
Move.

687
00:48:25,501 --> 00:48:26,905
Honestly.

688
00:48:27,068 --> 00:48:30,074
Mom, just ignore people like him.

689
00:48:30,106 --> 00:48:32,448
No. You have to shut people
like him down early.

690
00:48:32,473 --> 00:48:34,021
That's what items are for.

691
00:48:34,046 --> 00:48:35,342
You're supposed to use them.

692
00:48:35,367 --> 00:48:37,851
He lost because he's bad at it,
and now he's picking a fight?

693
00:48:38,849 --> 00:48:39,872
Well?

694
00:48:39,897 --> 00:48:41,778
He's asking for a real-life fight.

695
00:48:41,881 --> 00:48:43,447
Don't give him our address.

696
00:48:43,472 --> 00:48:45,792
What if he comes after us?

697
00:48:45,817 --> 00:48:48,946
People like that are all bark and no bite.

698
00:48:48,971 --> 00:48:50,823
They just act tough from behind a screen.

699
00:48:50,990 --> 00:48:53,903
But what if he really finds us?

700
00:48:53,928 --> 00:48:56,491
Don't worry. You've got me.

701
00:48:56,531 --> 00:48:59,725
I'll protect you,
so don't give it another thought.

702
00:49:00,099 --> 00:49:03,477
He's obviously just a little kid.
What does he think he's doing?

703
00:49:03,598 --> 00:49:04,923
What school does he go to?

704
00:49:06,238 --> 00:49:08,189
You messed with the wrong person.

705
00:49:08,464 --> 00:49:10,746
Let's settle this once and for all.

706
00:49:13,672 --> 00:49:15,642
See? I told you not to come.

707
00:49:15,838 --> 00:49:17,506
No. It was fun.

708
00:49:17,629 --> 00:49:19,498
Where else do I get a show
like that for free?

709
00:49:19,785 --> 00:49:22,820
I've known you since you were twelve,
and today I saw a whole new side of you.

710
00:49:23,098 --> 00:49:25,268
Completely adorable and human.

711
00:49:26,190 --> 00:49:28,057
- Go on in.
- Hold on.

712
00:49:32,234 --> 00:49:35,584
Mom, I'm at the door.
Is there anything to eat?

713
00:49:36,390 --> 00:49:38,393
Yes, got it. I'll be right up.

714
00:49:39,931 --> 00:49:41,583
Since you're here, stay for dinner.

715
00:49:41,831 --> 00:49:43,863
You like my mom's cooking.

716
00:49:44,370 --> 00:49:46,886
What's so great about him
that you even feed him?

717
00:49:47,106 --> 00:49:48,251
Good evening, sir.

718
00:49:48,276 --> 00:49:49,628
Dad.

719
00:49:51,308 --> 00:49:52,991
What? Am I wrong?

720
00:49:54,231 --> 00:49:56,194
A man who treats my daughter
like leftovers,

721
00:49:56,361 --> 00:49:58,934
why would I feed him a warm meal?

722
00:49:59,539 --> 00:50:02,273
Why are you doing this?

723
00:50:02,706 --> 00:50:05,649
Why do you keep sending mixed signals?

724
00:50:06,797 --> 00:50:08,192
Why walk her home,

725
00:50:08,217 --> 00:50:10,439
and why agree to eat her mother's food?

726
00:50:11,927 --> 00:50:14,862
- It's not like that, Dad.
- Stay out of it.

727
00:50:15,011 --> 00:50:16,116
He has a mouth of his own.

728
00:50:16,651 --> 00:50:19,474
With respect, I've never sent
Seo Hyeon mixed signals, sir.

729
00:50:20,382 --> 00:50:22,598
Really? He didn't confuse you?

730
00:50:22,675 --> 00:50:25,299
He's right. I asked him to walk me home,

731
00:50:25,324 --> 00:50:28,902
and I offered him dinner
to thank him for it.

732
00:50:28,927 --> 00:50:30,997
Dad, you don't know anything.

733
00:50:32,257 --> 00:50:34,111
This makes me angrier.

734
00:50:34,363 --> 00:50:37,127
What are you lacking that you keep
throwing yourself at someone like him?

735
00:50:37,871 --> 00:50:39,599
And what makes you so special?

736
00:50:39,624 --> 00:50:41,024
Is Seo Hyeon not good enough for you?

737
00:50:41,345 --> 00:50:43,931
Not at all, sir. Absolutely not.

738
00:50:43,956 --> 00:50:45,042
- She isn't?
- No, sir.

739
00:50:45,076 --> 00:50:47,342
You never led her on.

740
00:50:47,367 --> 00:50:48,681
This is your problem.

741
00:50:49,590 --> 00:50:51,024
Dad.

742
00:50:52,112 --> 00:50:54,024
He's hopeless.

743
00:50:55,437 --> 00:50:58,474
You're supposed to keep
the other person guessing,

744
00:50:58,658 --> 00:51:01,210
push a little, let them push back,

745
00:51:01,235 --> 00:51:05,440
then pull them in.
What are you, a stone wall?

746
00:51:05,691 --> 00:51:08,813
Just sitting there sealed up tight.

747
00:51:09,770 --> 00:51:11,167
It's maddening.

748
00:51:11,919 --> 00:51:13,635
- No food. Off you go.
- Yes, sir.

749
00:51:13,698 --> 00:51:16,489
- Dad!
- I'll be in touch again.

750
00:51:16,783 --> 00:51:18,135
Goodnight, sir.

751
00:51:22,723 --> 00:51:24,458
Take the same lift. Hurry.

752
00:51:51,529 --> 00:51:52,745
Sweetheart.

753
00:51:53,304 --> 00:51:56,077
- Do you like it?
- Yes.

754
00:51:57,551 --> 00:51:59,979
Marry me, Gyu Yeong.

755
00:52:01,058 --> 00:52:02,346
Marry you?

756
00:52:03,404 --> 00:52:04,676
I'll...

757
00:52:07,751 --> 00:52:10,199
pull down the stars and the moon for you,

758
00:52:10,455 --> 00:52:12,215
and make you truly happy.

759
00:52:13,797 --> 00:52:16,434
Please marry me.

760
00:52:25,228 --> 00:52:27,141
Will you marry me?

761
00:52:30,386 --> 00:52:31,556
Yes.

762
00:52:39,217 --> 00:52:40,468
It's beautiful.

763
00:52:46,289 --> 00:52:49,811
- I love you.
- I love you too.

764
00:52:51,461 --> 00:52:53,117
It suits you so well.

765
00:53:05,469 --> 00:53:07,157
So beautiful. Does it look good?

766
00:53:07,376 --> 00:53:08,940
Those were the days.

767
00:53:09,171 --> 00:53:11,166
I had a time like that once too.

768
00:53:14,119 --> 00:53:17,928
Everything good and lovely
seems to vanish too fast.

769
00:53:21,565 --> 00:53:22,964
It hasn't vanished.

770
00:53:24,638 --> 00:53:26,443
It's all still here with you.

771
00:53:27,371 --> 00:53:29,056
Here,

772
00:53:29,897 --> 00:53:31,174
and here,

773
00:53:32,272 --> 00:53:33,514
and here.

774
00:53:34,589 --> 00:53:36,276
Honestly.

775
00:53:45,671 --> 00:53:47,637
Why is it suddenly so warm in here?

776
00:53:48,791 --> 00:53:50,436
Shall we go up now?

777
00:53:50,798 --> 00:53:52,563
I'd like to rest a bit.

778
00:53:54,167 --> 00:53:56,356
Just let me finish this. Cheers.

779
00:54:01,429 --> 00:54:03,833
Sweetheart, are you all right?

780
00:54:04,151 --> 00:54:06,123
I'll just pop to the restroom.

781
00:54:06,184 --> 00:54:07,636
- Wait here.
- Sure.

782
00:54:10,164 --> 00:54:12,261
When did you even arrange all this?

783
00:54:14,616 --> 00:54:15,913
Does it suit me?

784
00:54:22,643 --> 00:54:26,086
Even being generous,
she looks a dozen years older than you.

785
00:54:26,639 --> 00:54:28,048
You've got strange taste.

786
00:54:33,922 --> 00:54:35,277
Mind your own business.

787
00:54:36,849 --> 00:54:38,325
Looks like you got a ring,

788
00:54:38,350 --> 00:54:39,891
you're not actually marrying him?

789
00:54:40,224 --> 00:54:41,451
Mind your own business.

790
00:54:42,091 --> 00:54:43,468
And if I do?

791
00:54:45,169 --> 00:54:47,323
Did the size of that diamond blind you?

792
00:54:48,575 --> 00:54:50,440
You think this is my first ring?

793
00:54:52,558 --> 00:54:53,986
Are you really getting married?

794
00:54:54,078 --> 00:54:56,090
I'm considering it favorably.

795
00:54:56,771 --> 00:55:00,060
His face is decent enough,
his education isn't bad,

796
00:55:00,504 --> 00:55:03,586
and above all, he has serious money.

797
00:55:04,889 --> 00:55:06,277
You don't care about character?

798
00:55:06,506 --> 00:55:09,876
He has enough money that I don't have to.
Satisfied?

799
00:55:13,523 --> 00:55:14,929
Have you saved anything?

800
00:55:15,577 --> 00:55:18,620
A guy I know from a host bar
even bought an apartment.

801
00:55:24,584 --> 00:55:25,935
That's what you wanted to say?

802
00:55:26,784 --> 00:55:28,320
Easy come, easy go.

803
00:55:28,504 --> 00:55:30,724
Don't blow it just because it comes easy.

804
00:55:30,741 --> 00:55:32,323
Buy yourself a studio at least.

805
00:55:32,348 --> 00:55:34,770
You're the first person
to find out what I do,

806
00:55:36,861 --> 00:55:38,462
and that's what you want to say?

807
00:55:42,331 --> 00:55:43,630
What should I say, then?

808
00:55:44,178 --> 00:55:46,339
Of all the jobs out there,
why become a kept man?

809
00:55:46,422 --> 00:55:48,206
Should I faint from the shock?

810
00:55:48,718 --> 00:55:50,024
Do I look like Han Gyu Rim?

811
00:55:53,787 --> 00:55:56,916
Forget it. I'm the fool for asking.

812
00:56:04,291 --> 00:56:05,655
Little brat.

813
00:56:06,647 --> 00:56:08,542
Of all the jobs out there.

814
00:56:10,466 --> 00:56:11,707
Whatever.

815
00:56:12,142 --> 00:56:13,920
It's his life, not mine.

816
00:56:22,521 --> 00:56:24,726
- Mom.
- Yes?

817
00:56:25,695 --> 00:56:28,932
What was Dad like?

818
00:56:35,015 --> 00:56:36,508
Why bring that up now?

819
00:56:37,450 --> 00:56:38,671
No reason.

820
00:56:38,829 --> 00:56:41,608
My teacher asked about him earlier...

821
00:56:42,024 --> 00:56:43,525
and I had nothing to say.

822
00:56:45,535 --> 00:56:49,278
Honestly, I've never cared before.

823
00:56:51,323 --> 00:56:53,529
And I probably won't going forward,

824
00:56:55,236 --> 00:56:58,338
so you don't have to tell me
if you'd rather not.

825
00:56:58,998 --> 00:57:01,235
I'm not dying to know or anything.

826
00:57:03,636 --> 00:57:06,916
He's your dad,
so he must be a good person, right?

827
00:57:08,097 --> 00:57:10,748
What else? Is he handsome?

828
00:57:11,097 --> 00:57:13,453
Is he tall? Does he look like me?

829
00:57:14,104 --> 00:57:16,020
He's handsome. Tall, too.

830
00:57:16,588 --> 00:57:18,643
Does he look like you? Let me see.

831
00:57:23,139 --> 00:57:24,470
You do look alike.

832
00:57:28,066 --> 00:57:30,090
Is he even still alive?

833
00:57:31,598 --> 00:57:32,744
Yes.

834
00:57:33,182 --> 00:57:34,831
Then do you...

835
00:57:35,476 --> 00:57:37,195
miss him?

836
00:57:38,588 --> 00:57:40,613
Do you miss him, Gyeol?

837
00:57:45,823 --> 00:57:46,971
No.

838
00:57:50,529 --> 00:57:53,515
I just need you.

839
00:58:15,403 --> 00:58:16,837
(Geumje Police, respect and consideration,
community safety with our residents)

840
00:58:16,862 --> 00:58:19,266
The stress had me out of my mind.

841
00:58:19,931 --> 00:58:22,567
I think my emotions got the better of me.

842
00:58:23,163 --> 00:58:25,407
I'm truly sorry for what I did.

843
00:58:28,087 --> 00:58:29,527
Will this do?

844
00:58:32,306 --> 00:58:33,523
Honestly.

845
00:58:36,133 --> 00:58:38,613
How badly do you have to swear
at a game...

846
00:58:38,702 --> 00:58:40,973
to get reported and hauled
in for questioning?

847
00:58:42,971 --> 00:58:46,098
I looked it up. These almost never
become formal investigations.

848
00:58:46,391 --> 00:58:48,441
How bad was it?

849
00:58:48,558 --> 00:58:50,441
I'm a victim too, you know.

850
00:58:50,771 --> 00:58:54,528
I took so much abuse at that screen
I wasn't crying tears,

851
00:58:54,727 --> 00:58:58,314
- I was crying blood.
- Right. Well done.

852
00:58:58,445 --> 00:59:02,638
Swearing and getting sworn at,
then hauled in for questioning together.

853
00:59:03,184 --> 00:59:06,449
- You two are practically soulmates.
- How old is he?

854
00:59:06,483 --> 00:59:09,473
Never mind his age.
Tell that soulmate of yours...

855
00:59:09,603 --> 00:59:13,178
that you're a bit unwell mentally
and ask him to let it go,

856
00:59:13,308 --> 00:59:14,697
then settle it amicably.

857
00:59:19,986 --> 00:59:22,466
Why? Want a lawyer? Shall I come?

858
00:59:22,727 --> 00:59:25,817
No, I'm fine. I'm off.

859
00:59:32,335 --> 00:59:34,274
What, does he think he's Benjamin Button?

860
00:59:35,651 --> 00:59:37,024
It's worse than that.

861
00:59:37,670 --> 00:59:39,266
How is he getting more immature?

862
00:59:39,611 --> 00:59:40,751
Forget it.

863
00:59:40,811 --> 00:59:42,024
Don't come back.

864
01:01:06,217 --> 01:01:07,581
Mr. Kim Mu Jin?

865
01:01:08,735 --> 01:01:09,825
Yes.

866
01:01:10,903 --> 01:01:13,660
Then you must be Han Gyeol's...

867
01:01:14,748 --> 01:01:16,024
guardian?

868
01:01:18,309 --> 01:01:23,151
The account is Gyeol's,
but the swearing was mine.

869
01:01:23,479 --> 01:01:26,898
I see. You're both old enough
to know better.

870
01:01:27,697 --> 01:01:29,171
Please take a seat, both of you.

871
01:01:36,731 --> 01:01:38,795
"You absolute piece of work,"

872
01:01:39,131 --> 01:01:43,134
"watching you, I feel awful
for the mother who gave birth to you,"

873
01:01:43,391 --> 01:01:46,591
"ten months of suffering
for a piece of trash."

874
01:01:46,788 --> 01:01:47,997
Ms. Han Gyu Rim.

875
01:01:48,419 --> 01:01:50,170
Did you actually say this?

876
01:01:52,171 --> 01:01:53,236
Yes.

877
01:01:54,911 --> 01:01:56,324
And Mr. Kim Mu Jin,

878
01:01:56,786 --> 01:01:58,828
"You absolute waste of space."

879
01:01:59,111 --> 01:02:01,868
"Instead of worrying about my mother,
worry about your own."

880
01:02:01,984 --> 01:02:03,588
"Is she even alive?"

881
01:02:03,911 --> 01:02:05,957
"Or did she pass from the shame already?"

882
01:02:06,163 --> 01:02:07,615
That's what you said.

883
01:02:08,088 --> 01:02:10,703
- Yes.
- What did you mean by this?

884
01:02:10,866 --> 01:02:12,495
Let's hear from each of you.

885
01:02:14,276 --> 01:02:16,259
There was no grand meaning.

886
01:02:16,314 --> 01:02:19,438
I think I lost my temper in the moment.

887
01:02:20,159 --> 01:02:22,742
Neither of you wants
the other prosecuted, correct?

888
01:02:23,422 --> 01:02:24,693
No.

889
01:02:25,476 --> 01:02:26,481
No.

890
01:02:26,531 --> 01:02:27,924
It's a first offense for you both,

891
01:02:28,647 --> 01:02:31,024
and you both seem remorseful,
so settle this between you,

892
01:02:31,171 --> 01:02:33,778
write letters of apology,
and exchange them.

893
01:02:34,211 --> 01:02:36,407
If you're reported for this again,

894
01:02:36,513 --> 01:02:38,050
it won't end this way next time.

895
01:02:38,718 --> 01:02:40,610
- Yes.
- Understood.

896
01:02:40,823 --> 01:02:42,094
Let me think.

897
01:02:42,971 --> 01:02:45,851
Not here. Both of you, follow me.

898
01:02:55,215 --> 01:02:57,960
Call me when you've finished
your apology letters.

899
01:03:13,653 --> 01:03:16,880
- Excuse me...
- Just write it and go.

900
01:04:06,851 --> 01:04:08,024
Planning to run again?

901
01:04:12,191 --> 01:04:13,788
If you're going to run, do it properly,

902
01:04:14,531 --> 01:04:16,024
so we never have to meet like this.

903
01:04:24,382 --> 01:04:25,708
Mom.

904
01:04:26,912 --> 01:04:28,024
My boy.

905
01:04:32,415 --> 01:04:34,756
Mom, that must have been so hard.

906
01:04:35,947 --> 01:04:39,266
Gyeol kept saying he wanted to see you,
so I brought him along.

907
01:04:39,617 --> 01:04:40,970
Did everything go all right?

908
01:04:43,188 --> 01:04:44,404
Here, eat this.

909
01:04:45,884 --> 01:04:47,948
You shouldn't have.

910
01:05:18,541 --> 01:05:21,024
(Love on the Menu)

911
01:05:21,291 --> 01:05:23,149
Let's go, honey.

912
01:05:23,239 --> 01:05:24,916
So that man is her husband?

913
01:05:24,941 --> 01:05:26,377
She's gone and married too?

914
01:05:26,419 --> 01:05:28,508
- He wants to start over?
- Hey!

915
01:05:28,533 --> 01:05:30,371
So the feelings are still there.

916
01:05:30,396 --> 01:05:32,351
You never got over him.

917
01:05:32,376 --> 01:05:35,266
- She has a son too?
- Eight years old, apparently.

918
01:05:35,291 --> 01:05:37,539
Han Gyu Rim broke up with Mu Jin
eight years ago.

919
01:05:37,564 --> 01:05:41,797
You'd only have to pretend to be my father
once. Actually, just twice.

920
01:05:41,822 --> 01:05:43,375
Let's go shopping for clothes
at the department store.

921
01:05:43,414 --> 01:05:44,936
Why clothes all of a sudden?

922
01:05:45,012 --> 01:05:48,271
- For meeting the in-laws.
- Who's meeting in-laws?

923
01:05:48,419 --> 01:05:50,814
- Gyu Yeong.
- What?

924
01:05:51,506 --> 01:05:53,506
Dramaday.me
